# A blow struck on the run, at a target that stands still ahead: the damage's
# scale is how fast the player moves ahead against how fast they run (a full run
# is 1, and then the damage is the tag's 50 to 60, rolled), and the player goes on
# running through the blow (the engine's blow has no lunge of its own: the
# simulation's movement matches it to the last bit). One blow is enough: the
# shield, which takes a blow's damage and a bit more, is nearly gone.
scenario melee_running
map bloodgulch
start flat_field 77.9 -166.2 0.32 0.0
target 81.3 -166.2 0.32 3.14159265
weapon weapons/pistol/pistol
ticks 200
# aim at the body
input 0 200 pitch=-0.2
input 30 66 forward=1.0
input 60 61 melee=1
# (a run's speed is held to a last digit of the engine's, as the walking scenarios do)

tolerance position 0
tolerance velocity 0.005
tolerance facing 0
tolerance state 0
tolerance rounds 0
tolerance heat 0
tolerance shield 0
tolerance body 0
tolerance stun 0
tolerance life 0
tolerance hit 0
tolerance shots 0
tolerance age 0
